  "notes": "A single open limestone vault spans Shaharah’s narrow rocky gorge. The model follows the mapped footbridge, with a shallow stepped deck, rough parapets, a west gateway, small retaining-wall arches, and stairs along the east cliff. The named PMTiles footbridge and connected paths fix the placement and signed alignment. Vault dimensions, stair rise, gate profile, and stonework are exterior photo interpretations. The elevation grid flattens the slot under the bridge. A small authored relief patch reconstructs that slot and blends into the sampled terrain. Its rock detail and gorge depth are visualization approximations.",
